  "notes": "`&[u8]` carries Go's possibly-invalid UTF-8: `rust_stdlib::text::BytesExt` adds the Go functions std lacks for byte slices (invalid bytes are U+FFFD of width 1; case mapping, title casing and folding use rust_stdlib::unicode's Go tables, exact on every rune and compared by tools/bytes_check.py), and std slice methods are used where semantics match. Buffer and Reader keep Go's unread rules and capacity growth. Go index -1 is None; nil-versus-empty slices are not distinguished.",
